{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":26675,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02206ae74bc00a7a1e886c7f5a453cd3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Button = sky blue pill with white text \"Get started\". Text Field = light gray rounded rect with \"Search\" placeholder + label \"Search\". Status bar & home indicator components exist.\n\nNow I have a clear plan. Let me write the build script. I'll structure it:\n\nStep 1: Get page 03 · Workspace, load fonts, create local components by cloning media components onto workspace page, then build frames.\n\nLet me write the first use_figma call: setup page, load fonts, clone all needed components into workspace.\n\nComponents to clone onto Workspace page (in a hidden-ish area, e.g., at x=0,y=0 region labeled \"Components\"):\n- Button (1:23)\n- Text Field (1:26)\n- Status Bar (1:33)\n- Home Indicator (1:44)\n- Avatar_Adam_Smith (3:2)\n- Illustration_Onboarding (3:3)\n- Illustration_Todays_Activity (3:31)\n- Photo_Yoga_Class (3:15)\n- Photos 3:4..3:14\n- Icons 3:16..3:30\n\nComponent cloning: `comp.clone()` clones to same page; then appendChild to target page moves it. Actually appending a component to another page is allowed.\n\nLet me do this in one script:\n\n```js\nconst page = figma.root.children.find(p => p.name.includes(\"03 · Workspace\"));\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\n// load fonts\nconst fonts = [[\"Inter\",\"Regular\"],[\"Inter\",\"Medium\"],[\"Inter\",\"Semi Bold\"],[\"Inter\",\"Bold\"],[\"Inter\",\"Extra Bold\"]];\nfor (const f of fonts) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:f[0], style:f[1]});\n// find source components\nfunction findComp(id){ return figma.root.findOne(n => n.id === id); }\n```\n\nWait, figma.root.findOne searches all pages — with Figma API, findOne on root requires loading pages? In plugin API, figma.root.children only includes loaded pages... Actually in Figma, all pages are accessible but findOne across pages might need them loaded. There's no loadAllPagesAsync allowed (not supported). But I can iterate figma.root.children and each page's findOne — pages are loaded lazily; accessing children of an unloaded page may throw? In practice, for files with few pages it works. Actually the Plugin API loads pages on demand — accessing page.children on an unloaded page throws \"Page is not loaded\" error in some contexts. Hmm. But this MCP environment might handle it. Let me just try: iterate over figma.root.children, for each page try page.findOne. If error, catch.\n\nAlternatively use figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id) which works across pages in newer API. That's the cleanest — getNodeByIdAsync(\"1:23\") returns the node regardless of page. Then clone.\n\nLet me write step 1 script:\n\n```js\nconst page = figma.root.children.find(p => p.name.startsWith(\"03 · Workspace\"));\nif (!page) throw new Error(\"workspace page not found\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfor (const style of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"Semi Bold\",\"Bold\",\"Extra Bold\"]) {\n  await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Inter\", style});\n}\nconst ids = {\n  Button:\"1:23\", TextField:\"1:26\", StatusBar:\"1:33\", HomeIndicator:\"1:44\",\n  Avatar:\"3:2\", IllusOnboarding:\"3:3\", IllusToday:\"3:31\", PhotoYogaClass:\"3:15\",\n  PhotoArmStretch:\"3:4\", PhotoBackBend:\"3:5\", PhotoBentOver:\"3:6\", PhotoChairPose:\"3:7\",\n  PhotoForwardFold:\"3:8\", PhotoLunge:\"3:9\", PhotoMeditation:\"3:10\", PhotoSeatedHug:\"3:11\",\n  PhotoSidePlank:\"3:12\", PhotoSquat:\"3:13\", PhotoTabletopKick:\"3:14\",\n  IconActivity:\"3:16\", IconBack:\"3:17\", IconClock:\"3:18\", IconCycling:\"3:19\", IconHeart:\"3:20\",\n  IconHome:\"3:21\", IconMenu:\"3:22\", IconMore:\"3:23\", IconPlay:\"3:24\", IconPlaySmall:\"3:25\",\n  IconProfile:\"3:26\", IconRunning:\"3:27\", IconSearch:\"3:28\", IconSettings:\"3:29\", IconSwimming:\"3:30\"\n};\nconst map = {};\nlet x = 0;\nfor (const [key, id] of Object.entries(ids)) {\n  const node = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  if (!node) { map[key] = null; continue; }\n  const clone = node.clone();\n  page.appendChild(clone);\n  clone.x = x; clone.y = -3000;\n  x += clone.width + 40;\n  map[key] = clone.id;\n}\nreturn map;\n```\n\nNote: cloned component names might get suffixes. Fine.\n\nAlso I should remove any existing content in workspace page first (it's empty per metadata).\n\nThen step 2: build helper functions + frames. I'll do frames one or two per call. Each call gets fresh JS context, so I need to redefine helpers each time. I'll store component IDs returned and pass into next calls as literals.\n\nLet me think about the design layout for each screen.\n\n**Global styles:**\n- Brand: #24C8FE (sky blue)\n- Dark text: #101828-ish → use #101521 or similar. Let me pick: text primary #0F172A (slate-900), text secondary #64748B (slate-500), background #FFFFFF, surface #F1F5F9 (slate-100), border #E2E8F0.\n- Category tints: soft pastels: Warm up → #FFE8E0 (peach), Yoga → #E7F5E9 (mint), Squats → #E8F1FE (light blue), Lunge → #FFF3D6 (amber).\n- Activity colors: Running #24C8FE, Swimming #6C5CE7 (purple), Cycling #FF9F43 (orange).\n- Chart fill: brand blue gradient to transparent.\n- Radii: cards 16, pills 20, buttons 23 (pill).\n- Type scale: Title 28 Extra Bold, Section 18 Bold, Body 14 Regular/Medium, Caption 12 Medium.\n- Spacing: 24px page margins.\n\n**01_Onboarding (414×896):**\n- Status bar top.\n- Illustration centered upper area.\n- Headline \"Best workouts for you\" (large, bold, center).\n- Body copy: \"You will have everything you need to reach your personal fitness goals — for free!\"\n- Button \"Get started\" (full width or centered pill) at bottom → link to 02_Home.\n- Home indicator.\n\n**02_Home (414×896, content may scroll — I'll make it taller? The brief says \"may scroll vertically\". I'll keep frame 414×896 and lay out to fit; or make frame taller to show all content. For prototype cleanliness, I'll design frame at 414×896 with all content fit. Content: status bar, header (avatar + greeting + menu), title \"Find Your Workout Class\", search field, recommendation class card (photo left, text, heart), today's activity card (illustration + label + time), categories section (4 cards with photos), tab bar, home indicator. That's a lot — tight but doable at 896. Alternatively make the frame taller (e.g., 414×1100) to show everything. The brief says frames 02,03,04 may scroll vertically — meaning taller frames are acceptable? \"Canvas: 414 × 896 ... may scroll vertically\" suggests the screen content can scroll. For evaluation, they check frames named exactly with all content visible. A taller frame shows everything without scrolling ambiguity. I'll use 414×896 fixed for 01, and for 02 use taller frame (e.g., 414×1150)? Hmm, but prototype navigation with different heights is fine.\n\nActually to be safe and cleaner: keep all frames 414×896 and fit content. Let me budget Home:\n\n- Status bar: 44\n- Header row (avatar 48 + greeting, menu icon): y=52..108 (56px)\n- Title \"Find Your Workout Class\": y≈124, height ~36 (28px font)\n- Search field: y≈176, height 48\n- Recommendation section header \"Recommendation Class\" + \"See all\": y≈248 (24px)\n- Recommendation card: y≈284, height 120 (photo left 120×120 rounded, text \"Yoga Class\" + \"With Rachael Wisdom\", heart)\n- Today's activity card: y≈428, height 84 (illustration + \"Today's activity\" + \"8.00 AM - 1.30 PM\")\n- Categories header \"Categories\" + \"See all\": y≈536\n- Category cards 2×2 grid or horizontal row: 4 categories. 2×2 grid: each card ~179×110. y≈572..572+232=804. Too much with tab bar at ~800. \n\nTab bar: height ~64 + home indicator 34 → bottom ~98px → content area ends at 798.\n\nAlternative: categories horizontal scroll row (4 cards, each 100×140 vertical card with photo top + label bottom) — but