 → 04. I'll also wire Home tab on 03 → 02 for completeness (harmless). Actually \"Entry only (no frame)\" lists Profile and Settings tabs as entry-only, implying Home/Activity tabs navigate. I'll wire Home and Activity tabs on all three frames appropriately.)\n\n**Components to build in workspace (reusable):**\nBuild local components: TabBar (with variants? simpler: one component, instances with current tab swapped manually — but component reuse is evaluated; create component \"Tab Bar\" and use instances, overriding icon colors per instance? Overrides of fill color inside instances are allowed). Simpler: create TabBar component with default (Home active), then for Activity-active frame, instance and override colors. That demonstrates reuse.\n\nAlso create components: Category Card, Exercise Row, Activity Card, Day Pill, Class Card, Tag, Icon Button, Search Field (instance of cloned Text Field), Section Header. To manage scope, I'll build these as components in a \"Design System\" frame on workspace page, then instantiate into screens.\n\nGiven effort constraints, plan components:\n1. `DS / Tab Bar` — auto-layout row of 4 tab items (each icon+label), Home active default.\n2. `DS / Section Header` — title left, \"See all\" right.\n3. `DS / Category Card` — tint bg, label, photo slot. Instances override photo + bg tint + label.\n4. `DS / Class Card` — recommendation card.\n5. `DS / Today Card` — today's activity.\n6. `DS / Exercise Row` — thumbnail, name, duration, play.\n7. `DS / Day Pill` — day label + date, default state; selected override.\n8. `DS / Activity Card` — icon + name + stats.\n9. `DS / Tag` — icon + text pill.\n10. `DS / Icon Button` — circle with icon (back/more/heart/menu).\n\nThat's a lot of component work. Use auto-layout where easy, else absolute positioning (faster for cards). I'll use plain frames with absolute children for cards (quicker to compute), and mark them as components.\n\nHonestly, to manage complexity, I'll build components with absolute layout and simple structure.\n\n**Chart:** draw with vector path or bars. A smooth curve is doable via vector network but complex via API. Bars are easier: 5 vertical bars at 8AM,10AM,12PM,2PM,4PM with varying heights, 4PM tallest/selected in brand color with tooltip \"120 cal\". Brief says \"Chart: hourly calories ... (curve values illustrative)\" — a bar chart satisfies \"chart\". But \"curve values\" hints original was a curve. Bars are fine and illustrative. I'll do rounded bars + a tooltip pill above 4PM saying \"120 cal\". Add a horizontal baseline.\n\nNow, photos on category cards: photos are transparent cut-outs; place scaled instance on tinted card. Instance scaling: set rescale via `instance.scale`? Use `instance.rescale()`? For instances, use `instance.resize(w,h)` — allowed (may distort; better use scale factor via rescale). `instance.rescale(0.5)` scales proportionally. Photos wide are 240×160 (3:2), tall 107×160. Category photo mapping:\n- Warm up → Photo_Seated_Hug (tall)\n- Yoga → Photo_Meditation (tall)\n- Squats → Photo_Squat (wide)\n- Lunge → Photo_Lunge (wide)\n\nCategory card 177×108: tall photo scaled to height ~88 (width ~59), positioned bottom-right; wide photo height ~70 → width 105, bottom-right. Label top-left 16px SemiBold. \n\nExercise thumbnails: rows h=64: thumb 56×56 rounded 12 with light tint bg + photo scaled to fit (~40×52 for tall, 52×35 wide). Photo per exercise from data:\n1. Forward_Fold (wide) 02.30\n2. Chair_Pose (tall) 02.00\n3. Side_Plank (tall) 03.20\n4. Bent_Over (wide) 02.30\n5. Meditation (tall) 05.30\n6. Seated_Hug (tall) 06.10\n7. Lunge (wide) 04.50\n8. Arm_Stretch (tall) 03.30\n9. Back_Bend (tall) 01.30\n10. Tabletop_Kick (wide) 05.20\n\nRecommendation card: Photo_Yoga_Class is a real photo 200×160 — crop into 110×96? resize to cover: scale to height 96 → width 120. Use a mask: place instance in a rounded rect frame with clipsContent. Actually simpler: make card layout: left image area 120×120 with clipsContent, instance inside scaled; right side text \"Yoga Class\" (16 SemiBold), \"With Rachael Wisdom\" (12 Regular gray), heart icon button top-right.\n\nVideo cover (03): card 366×184, Photo_Seated_Hug centered, play button (white circle 56 with brand play icon? or brand circle with white play). Use Icon_Play instance recolored white inside brand circle. Also gradient overlay bottom for style.\n\nTags: pill: bg #F1F5F9, icon 14 + text 13 Medium gray-dark. \"37.10 mins\" with clock, \"Running\" with running icon.\n\nIcons recoloring: icon components have their own colors; recolor by setting fills on their vector children within instances. Instance children fills can be overridden. I'll write helper `tintIcon(inst, hex)` that walks descendants and sets fills to solid color.\n\nStatus bar glyphs: black on light bg — default is black, fine. On video cover area? Status bar sits above content on white; fine.\n\nTab bar: 4 items; active: brand color icon + label + small dot? Keep simple: active icon brand, label brand SemiBold; inactive gray #94A3B8.\n\nNow the Button component (1:23): blue pill \"Get started\" — 161×46. For onboarding, make instance full-width 366 — instance resize allowed. Text inside may not stretch if no auto-layout; resizing instance may distort text position. Let me check: the Button component — I don't know its internal structure. Safer: put instance at natural size 161×46 centered? Design-wise full-width button nicer. I could inspect the button's children first. Let me do a quick read-only inspection call to get Button and TextField structure, then decide.\n\nAlso need to check TextField (1:26) — 374×75 includes label \"Search\" above field? From screenshot: label \"Search\" on top, field below with placeholder \"Search\". I might restyle: use instance as-is for Home search (label \"Search\" + field). Must include \"Search\" (Icon_Search). The given text field may not include the search icon. I'll build my own search field component: rounded rect bg #F1F5F9, Icon_Search left, placeholder \"Search\" gray. But brief says reuse given Text Field? \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\" — I should use Button and TextField instances at least once. Home needs a Search field — I'll use the cloned TextField instance and add Icon_Search inside? Modifying instance internals isn't allowed (can't add children to instance). Alternative: place TextField instance, and overlay search icon inside its box area. Or use TextField on Home as the search (its placeholder is \"Search\" and label \"Search\") and skip extra icon? Must-include says: Search: \"Search\" (Icon_Search) — icon required. I'll overlay the icon instance on top of the text field's left area (absolute positioned sibling). That satisfies reuse + icon.\n\nLet me inspect Button/TextField internals quickly with a read-only use_figma call. Also inspect one photo component to know fills (whether photos are image fills — recoloring icons only needed for icons).\n\nActually let me limit inspection: Button structure + TextField structure + one icon structure. One call.\n\nThen build. Total planned use_figma calls:\n1. Inspect components (read-only).\n2. Setup: page, fonts, clone all components to workspace, return id map.\n3. Create design-system components (tab bar, cards, etc.) — maybe 2 calls.\n4. Build 01_Onboarding + 02_Home — 1-2 calls.\n5. Build 03_Warm_Up — 1 call.\n6. Build 04_Activity — 1 call.\n7. Prototype wiring — 1 call.\n8. Screenshots + fixes — several.\n\nLet me start with inspection.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dd82475-447e-4a4a-b1d4-9abeb6ff2aa0","uuid":"c84af178-7b4f-4f4e-b575-c50cff41e9e0","timestamp":"2026-11-01T14:27:50.197Z","thinking_duration_ms":161716}
