at ~305-345 → actual 390-442?? That doesn't match 362-392. Unless the tags have larger height. The Tag component: auto layout horizontal, padding 8 top/bottom, content height 14 (icon 12, text ~15) → total ~30-31. Placed at 362 → ends ~392. Desc at 404. Screenshot shows desc text starting at ~330*... hmm the desc text in screenshot is at y≈320-350 → actual 410-448. OK maybe no overlap, just tight. But visually in the screenshot the chips look like they're at the same band as desc line 1. Eh — measured: chips bottom edge ~345*1.28 ≈ 442? I can't be precise. Let me just move desc down to 412 and give tags more breathing room. Actually the visible issue: desc first line \"Warm up properly before exercising to prevent injury...\" appears to START at the same height as the chips. Look again at the image: chips row is at y≈300-350 in the 700px image. Desc lines at 322-352. They DO overlap. \n\nWait — actually look carefully: the \"37.10 mins\" chip text is IN FRONT of desc text: \"Wa[37.10 mins]erly befo[Running]ising...\" Yes! Overlap confirmed. The desc text y=404 must actually be rendering higher because... hmm no. Unless tags are at 362 but with height ~31, they end at 393, and desc at 404 line-height 22 → first line occupies 404-426. Screenshot scale: 404*0.781 = 315, tags 362*0.781 = 283 to 306. The screenshot shows chips around y 300-350 though... \n\nHmm wait, maybe I'm misreading pixel positions. Regardless — visually there IS overlap in the screenshot. Let me just re-measure via API: get absolute positions of tags and desc text.\n\nActually, possible cause: tag auto-layout with counterAxisAlignItems CENTER, and text node inside has fontSize 12 → height ~15; icon 12. Padding 8. Total 31. That's what I assumed. Let me measure actual rendered heights via API and adjust.\n\nLet me also double check the 04 week strip day spacing: dx += 52.6 — 7 pills: 24 + 6*52.6 + 46 = 385.6 ✓ fits.\n\nAlso 04: value \"1.32 hours\" right column at x 268 w 70 right-aligned → text right edge at 338 = 366-16-12? Card width 366, right padding 16 → content right edge 350. Hmm I set x=268, w=70 → right edge 338, should be 350. Let me fix to x=280? Actually earlier fix set t.x = 268 with w 70 right aligned → right edge at 338. Should be 350 (366-16). Minor 12px misalignment. Fix: x=280 for right column, x=170 for left column (80 gap). Let me adjust: v1/u1 (hours): x=280, w=70 → right edge 350. v2/u2 (kilometers): x=170, w=70 → right edge 240. Screenshot shows values looking fine actually (\"1.32 hours\" right-ish, \"9.50 kilometers\" middle-right). Fine but let me align properly.\n\nPriority list:\n1. Fix 03 scroll structure + tag/desc overlap measurement.\n2. 02 strip horizontal scroll.\n3. 04 value column alignment (minor).\n4. Re-screenshot 03.\n5. Final check of reactions + IDs for report.\n\nLet me measure 03 first.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dd82475-447e-4a4a-b1d4-9abeb6ff2aa0","uuid":"d168e3d1-56d3-4dae-a3e2-2990c29450a2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T14:47:43.576Z","thinking_duration_ms":74683}
